Stock Market Prediction Using Machine Learning

Project Overview

I developed a machine learning project to investigate whether historical financial indicators could predict stock price movements over the next five trading days. I analyzed more than 27,000 historical stock observations across 10 publicly traded companies using Python.

Technologies Used

- Python
- Pandas and NumPy
- Scikit-learn
- Matplotlib
- Yahoo Finance (yfinance)

Machine Learning Models

I developed and evaluated two machine learning models:

- Logistic Regression: 59.28% accuracy
- Random Forest: 58.95% accuracy

I compared both models against a baseline accuracy of 59.28% and analyzed feature importance to identify relevant financial indicators.

Financial Indicators Analyzed

I incorporated several financial indicators, including:

- 20-day and 50-day moving averages
- Daily and weekly stock returns
- Historical volatility
- Trading volume

Investment Strategy Backtesting

I developed a stock selection strategy that ranked stocks based on their predicted probability of increasing in price.

I compared the three highest-ranked stocks against an equally weighted portfolio of all 10 companies.

Results:

| Metric | ML Strategy | Benchmark |
|---|---|---|
| Average 5-Day Return | 0.79% | 0.69% |
| Return Volatility | 2.96% | 2.01% |

The machine learning strategy generated slightly higher average historical returns but also experienced greater volatility.

Key Findings

My results demonstrated that machine learning can be applied to financial data to evaluate investment opportunities. However, the models did not meaningfully outperform a simple classification baseline.

The backtesting results were exploratory and did not account for transaction costs, overlapping holding periods, or the effects of refining models using the test period.

Future Improvements

I plan to explore additional financial indicators, company fundamentals, market sentiment, and more rigorous out-of-sample testing to improve model evaluation and investment strategy development.
